{"id":"bee0665ec95eaa96","group":"58","path":"58/batch06/58-cor-khinchine.md","title":"Khinchine's Inequality","display":"cor-khinchine — Khinchine's Inequality","type":"corollary","metadata":{"type":"corollary","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-cor-khinchine","aliases":["58-cor-khinchine"],"display":"cor-khinchine — Khinchine's Inequality","depends_on":["[[../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md]]","[[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md]]","[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"corollary"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-cor-khinchine"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-cor-khinchine</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"cor-khinchine — Khinchine's Inequality"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"8290c214ec3c85ca\" href=\"?note=8290c214ec3c85ca\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md\">../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"68427bc628af9b8d\" href=\"?note=68427bc628af9b8d\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md\">../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\land[0,1)\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\lambda([0,1))=1\">\\(\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\land[0,1)\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\lambda([0,1))=1\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"68427bc628af9b8d\" href=\"?note=68427bc628af9b8d\" title=\"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md\">../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1)\\;(r(n)(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor})\">\\(\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1)\\;(r(n)(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor})\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"8290c214ec3c85ca\" href=\"?note=8290c214ec3c85ca\" title=\"../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md\">../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md</a>, <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"36d7463d215be751\" href=\"?note=36d7463d215be751\" title=\"../batch16/58-df-function.md\">../batch16/58-df-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"a\\in\\mathbb R^N\">\\(a\\in\\mathbb R^N\\)</span> (有限系数向量)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}khinchine}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\land[0,1)\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\lambda([0,1))=1\\to\n\\forall p\\in[1,\\infty)\\;\\exists A_p,B_p\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall N\\in\\omega\\;\\forall a\\in\\mathbb R^N\\;\n\\left(A_p\\left(\\sum_{n&lt;N}|a(n)|^2\\right)^{1/2}\\leq\n\\left(\\int_{[0,1)}\\left|\\sum_{n&lt;N}a(n)r(n)(t)\\right|^p\\,d\\lambda(t)\\right)^{1/p}\n\\leq B_p\\left(\\sum_{n&lt;N}|a(n)|^2\\right)^{1/2}\\right)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}khinchine}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\land[0,1)\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\lambda([0,1))=1\\to\n\\forall p\\in[1,\\infty)\\;\\exists A_p,B_p\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall N\\in\\omega\\;\\forall a\\in\\mathbb R^N\\;\n\\left(A_p\\left(\\sum_{n&lt;N}|a(n)|^2\\right)^{1/2}\\leq\n\\left(\\int_{[0,1)}\\left|\\sum_{n&lt;N}a(n)r(n)(t)\\right|^p\\,d\\lambda(t)\\right)^{1/p}\n\\leq B_p\\left(\\sum_{n&lt;N}|a(n)|^2\\right)^{1/2}\\right)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Khinchine: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L^p\">\\(L^p\\)</span> norms of Rademacher sums are equivalent to Euclidean norm.</li>\n<li>Constants depend on <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"p\">\\(p\\)</span> only.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md","status":"resolved","id":"8290c214ec3c85ca","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md","status":"resolved","id":"68427bc628af9b8d","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch16/58-df-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md","status":"resolved","id":"68427bc628af9b8d","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\land[0,1)\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\lambda([0,1))=1$ (see [[../batch10/58-df-lebesgue.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md","status":"resolved","id":"8290c214ec3c85ca","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1)\\;(r(n)(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor})$ (see [[../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md]], [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch16/58-df-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"36d7463d215be751","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1)\\;(r(n)(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor})$ (see [[../batch20/58-df-rademacher.md]], [[../batch16/58-df-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\land[0,1)\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\lambda([0,1))=1","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Function}(r,\\omega,\\{-1,1\\}^{[0,1)})\\land\\forall n\\in\\omega\\;\\forall t\\in[0,1)\\;(r(n)(t)=(-1)^{\\lfloor2^{n+1}t\\rfloor})","display":false},{"tex":"a\\in\\mathbb R^N","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{cor\\text{-}khinchine}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{LebesgueMeasure}_S(\\lambda,\\mathcal L,\\mathbb R)\\land[0,1)\\in\\mathcal L\\land\\lambda([0,1))=1\\to\n\\forall p\\in[1,\\infty)\\;\\exists A_p,B_p\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall N\\in\\omega\\;\\forall a\\in\\mathbb R^N\\;\n\\left(A_p\\left(\\sum_{n<N}|a(n)|^2\\right)^{1/2}\\leq\n\\left(\\int_{[0,1)}\\left|\\sum_{n<N}a(n)r(n)(t)\\right|^p\\,d\\lambda(t)\\right)^{1/p}\n\\leq B_p\\left(\\sum_{n<N}|a(n)|^2\\right)^{1/2}\\right)","display":true},{"tex":"L^p","display":false},{"tex":"p","display":false}],"bytes":1346,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-68","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch06/58-cor-khinchine.md|58-cor-khinchine]]（batch06）"}],"outgoing":["8290c214ec3c85ca","68427bc628af9b8d","36d7463d215be751"]}